2. Structured SDK debug output (ADV-S3-8).
   Before the fix, structured.ts built the client with no debugLogger, and the
   SDK falls back to raw console when OPENROUTER_DEBUG is set
   (node_modules/@openrouter/sdk/esm/lib/sdks.js:60-61). The structured path
   therefore printed the Authorization header. 2d1c875e wires the shared
   redacting logger in (structured.ts:154). Now:
   - object arguments (request and response bodies) print "[body redacted]"
     (debug-logger.ts:44-47), so no prompt, answer, or response body on any
     path;
   - header strings keep the configured key forms redacted: raw key,
     trimmed key, and the bearer-stripped token, all length >= 8
     (debug-logger.ts:17-37);
   - retry adds no logging (retry.ts has no console call) and each attempt
     reuses the same redacting logger;
   - error mapping keeps HTTP errors status-only and applies redactApiKey to
     error text (providers.ts:41-77); route handlers log role plus status only;
   - usage records carry role, model, latency, tokens, outcome, status only
     (usage-log.ts:12-26).
   The ADV-S3-8 test proves the leak is closed: the mocked fetch asserts the
   wire header is "Bearer <KEY>" while the captured console output holds no
   key, prompt, or answer. It ran green in my full package heavy-run
   (165 of 165).

